  <running_head>FL. SCHUYL</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>abun-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">ligentiùs excultis, quæ Hippocratici</l>
    <l n="2">dogmatibus prorsus respondent, lucê</l>
    <l n="3">clariùs innotefcit. Unde sequitur Syl-</l>
    <l n="4">vium, cum de effervefcentia loquitur</l>
    <l n="5">sequi Hippocratis vestigia: &amp; quia</l>
    <l n="6">effervefcentia causa est plurimorum</l>
    <l n="7">naturalium, etiam præternaturalium</l>
    <l n="8">atque pravorum effectorum in hu-</l>
    <l n="9">mano corpore, quatenus naturaliter</l>
    <l n="10">sese habet, vel præternaturaliter est</l>
    <l n="11">auáta, imminuta, abolita aut deprava-</l>
    <l n="12">ta, hinc diarrhœæ, choleræ &amp; febres,</l>
    <l n="13">quæque præterea Hippocrates recen-</l>
    <l n="14">set, de Vet. Med. Text. xxxiv. rectè</l>
    <l n="15">igitur Sylvius præeunte Hippocrate</l>
    <l n="16">de effervefcentia sæpenumerò lo-</l>
    <l n="17">quitur, de qua præstitisset D.Le Vas-</l>
    <l n="18">seur tacuisse.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Pag. verò 11. paulò dilucidiori in-</l>
    <l n="20">tervallo, saltim aliquid dicere conatur:</l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>legitur, inquit, apud Hipp. naturam re-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>fingere invisibilem, non possibile: habi-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>tat namque mens cauta recessus, sacra-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>que ejus non minus quam θεῖα mysteriis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>abun-</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The page's left edge is cropped on several lines; a few letters at line ends are partly cut off, and "lucê" and "auáta" are uncertain readings marked by the scan. The Greek word "θεῖα" is approximate.</notes>
